Insight: Sales are heavily weighted toward large coastal population centers (NY, CA, FL, TX), which is expected, but the presence of South Carolina and Hawaii in the top 10 is notable and may warrant investigation into what's driving above-average performance in those smaller markets.
9. Underlying Data
The dashboard includes a filterable, row-level “Filtered Sales Data” table with fields: Retailer, Retailer ID, Invoice Date, Region, State, City, Product, Price per Unit, Units Sold, Total Sales, Operating Profit, Operating Margin, and Sales Method. This granularity supports drill-down analysis beyond the summary charts (e.g., by specific retailer, date, or product).
10. Summary Takeaways
•	Strong overall profitability (42.3% average margin) across a diversified retail footprint.
•	West region and West Gear retailer are the standout performers, both regionally and by profit contribution — a potential model to replicate elsewhere.
•	Early 2021 marked an inflection point in sales growth that merits root-cause investigation (e.g., new distribution deal, demand rebound, pricing changes).
•	Footwear outsells apparel, with men's street footwear as the top single category.
•	In-store and outlet channels dominate, suggesting an opportunity to grow the online channel if it can be scaled profitably.
•	Sales are concentrated in large states, but a few smaller states (South Carolina, Hawaii) show disproportionately strong performance worth a closer look.
Note: Figures for regional, product, retailer, and state charts are approximate, read from chart visuals rather than exact data labels. For precise figures, refer to the “Filtered Sales Data” table or export the underlying dataset from the dashboard.

